               Logical Operators
               =================


         0<n<10 is valid in maths 

         but in java it will give error  

         We use logical Operators in java to combine multiple conditions

         Therir are 3 logical Operators
         ===============================

        1. && LOGICAL AND
        2. || LOGICAL OR
        3. ! LOGICAL NOT

1.LOGICAL AND
================

conditions1             conditions2             Result

T                       T                        T

T                       F                        F

F                       T                        F

F                       F                        F



2.LOGICAL OR
==============

conditions1             conditions2             Result

T                       T                        T

T                       F                        T

F                       T                        T

F                       F                        F


example:1
==========

int a=10,b=5, c=15;

boolean d;

d= a>b && b>c;

SOP(d) ; //false

example:2
==========

int a=10,b=5, c=15;

boolean d;

d= a>b || b>c;

SOP(d) ; //true



3.LOGICAL NOT
==============

! Operator flips the boolean value , only works on boolean data.

Ex:
===

boolean a=false,b;
boolean c;
b=!a;
c=!b;
SOP(a);//  false
